// `>>`, the arithmetic shift, and the one whose over-shift is not zero.
//
// docs/SPEC.md 2.3 says a count at or past the width leaves the sign bit
// smeared across the whole word: all ones for a negative value, zero
// otherwise. A negative count would trap; here it returns zero, as it does for
// the other two shifts, and `z >= 0` is what keeps it out of the sign-fill
// case it would otherwise land in.

sar(word a, word z) {
  word v = 0;
  if(ult(z, 64) == 1) {
    v = sar_raw(a, z);
  } else if(a < 0 && z >= 0) {
    v = 0 - 1;
  }
} return word v;
